1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,420
Maria's a teacher, but she's not smart enough to know that eating junk food's bad for your health.

2
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:10,460
That's all she ever eats. She's gonna make herself sick.

3
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:13,900
It's not like we're the poster children for health food.

4
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:15,020
Sorry, what was that?

5
00:00:16,040 --> 00:00:20,060
As you know, you're fortunate enough to travel in the company of the Great Night Tribe.

6
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:23,760
If you keep spending your time hanging around an agent of the evil church,

7
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:25,760
I promise you it'll end in disaster.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:41,460
Since my other half is already awake, I figured it was only right that I got out of bed as well.

9
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:42,480
Plus, I'm starving.

10
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:43,700
Good timing, then.

11
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:47,980
Hmm. Looks like you've put together quite the feast this morning, haven't you?

12
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:52,380
It's not all for breakfast, actually. Some of it's for lunch.

13
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:54,740
Well, well. Cooking multiple meals?

14
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:57,180
What have you done with my bro?

15
00:00:57,180 --> 00:01:01,980
Well, have you finally recognized how awesome I am and decided to pay me the respect I'm clearly owed?

16
00:01:02,220 --> 00:01:04,060
I already told you this yesterday.

17
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:07,420
That Maria girl doesn't eat real food. All she ever eats is junk.

18
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:09,940
So I thought I'd help out by making her a decent meal.

19
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:13,660
But don't worry. I made enough for you, too.

20
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:18,880
So Maria's the priority, and I'm stuck here playing second fiddle.

21
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:20,040
What'd you say?

22
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:21,760
What do you care?

23
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:24,680
Hey, where are you running off to?

24
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:26,100
Your food will get cold.

25
00:01:26,660 --> 00:01:27,000
Cobito?

26
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:31,580
My brother's dumb. Big time.

27
00:03:01,806 --> 00:03:11,966
Hey! Didn't expect to see you so early.

28
00:03:12,146 --> 00:03:15,746
Not again. A person can't survive on potato chips alone.

29
00:03:15,926 --> 00:03:19,706
Speak for yourself. These taste way better than any of the other stuff they have here.

30
00:03:20,086 --> 00:03:20,946
Check it out!

31
00:03:21,606 --> 00:03:24,166
Whoa. That's a lot of chips.

32
00:03:24,966 --> 00:03:27,226
Yozura lets me stock up when I work for her.

33
00:03:27,406 --> 00:03:30,846
You're like a pack rat. Guess I shouldn't be surprised.

34
00:03:30,846 --> 00:03:31,846
Here.

35
00:03:35,146 --> 00:03:38,546
Oh, wow. Did you make all this just for me?

36
00:03:38,686 --> 00:03:42,306
That's very nice of you, but what's your angle, Kodika?

37
00:03:42,606 --> 00:03:44,166
People don't just make food.

38
00:03:44,346 --> 00:03:46,066
I don't have an angle, okay?

39
00:03:46,546 --> 00:03:48,246
Just make sure you return my box.

40
00:03:48,646 --> 00:03:50,186
I'll make your lunch for you tomorrow, too.

41
00:03:50,706 --> 00:03:54,586
Wow. You're really being nice to me out of the goodness of your heart.

42
00:03:54,986 --> 00:03:56,686
You must be some kind of saint.

43
00:03:57,046 --> 00:03:58,346
I don't know what it is.

44
00:03:58,346 --> 00:04:01,846
It's just that you sort of remind me of my sister when she was little.

45
00:04:02,146 --> 00:04:03,346
I want to look out for you.

46
00:04:04,046 --> 00:04:06,386
I didn't know you actually had a younger sister.

47
00:04:07,266 --> 00:04:10,146
I guess it makes sense. You are the big brother type.

48
00:04:10,546 --> 00:04:13,866
Yeah, well, I'd love to hang out, but I got to get to class.

49
00:04:14,206 --> 00:04:15,686
Lay off the potato chips, all right?

50
00:04:15,686 --> 00:04:18,346
Okay, big bro. You got it.

51
00:04:20,146 --> 00:04:21,006
Big bro?

52
00:04:22,566 --> 00:04:24,966
I've heard a lot of rumors about his dining habits.

53
00:04:25,286 --> 00:04:27,606
Apparently, he always eats his lunch before lunchtime.

54
00:04:29,226 --> 00:04:30,846
Please accept my apologies.

55
00:04:31,386 --> 00:04:34,086
I'm so sorry my snack didn't satisfy your hunger.

56
00:04:34,086 --> 00:04:36,866
That's not it, but thank you, though.

57
00:04:37,766 --> 00:04:38,986
Big brother, hey!

58
00:04:39,246 --> 00:04:39,826
Guess what?

59
00:04:40,046 --> 00:04:42,126
I ate my lunch and it was so awesome.

60
00:04:42,346 --> 00:04:45,806
Yozara's yucky potato chips taste like poo-poo compared to what you made.

61
00:04:46,006 --> 00:04:48,966
Poop head Yozara likes to make people eat nasty poo-poo chips.

62
00:04:49,086 --> 00:04:49,386
Oh.

63
00:04:49,506 --> 00:04:49,726
Oh!

64
00:04:49,726 --> 00:04:52,466
I was just kidding around. Your chips are the best.

65
00:04:53,366 --> 00:04:55,846
It's weird to make a young girl call you big bro.

66
00:04:56,046 --> 00:04:58,726
Do you have some kind of sexy little sister fetish or what?

67
00:04:58,846 --> 00:05:00,946
No, and I'm not making her call me anything.

68
00:05:01,186 --> 00:05:02,766
Kotika really is a big brother,

69
00:05:02,946 --> 00:05:05,146
so I figured it would be the perfect name for him.

70
00:05:10,286 --> 00:05:10,726
Gosh.

71
00:05:11,286 --> 00:05:13,686
Wouldn't it be awesome to go inside a video game?

72
00:05:15,366 --> 00:05:16,746
I mean, not really.

73
00:05:17,206 --> 00:05:19,126
That was a joke. I didn't really mean that.

74
00:05:19,126 --> 00:05:20,806
I just wanted to see the look on your face.

75
00:05:21,446 --> 00:05:22,446
Don't be embarrassed.

76
00:05:22,706 --> 00:05:24,646
Rika may not be able to get you into that game,

77
00:05:24,706 --> 00:05:25,646
but there's one she can.

78
00:05:25,966 --> 00:05:27,486
Rika has a different game you could play

79
00:05:27,486 --> 00:05:29,146
where you might have a similar experience.

80
00:05:29,906 --> 00:05:30,806
Are you serious?

81
00:05:31,326 --> 00:05:33,266
How in the world do you have something like that?

82
00:05:33,546 --> 00:05:35,326
After Rika helped them develop it,

83
00:05:35,426 --> 00:05:37,046
they let her keep a copy of the prototype.

84
00:05:38,046 --> 00:05:38,846
Want to try it out?

85
00:05:39,026 --> 00:05:40,086
Yeah, of course.

86
00:05:42,086 --> 00:05:43,546
So what? You put this on?

87
00:05:43,806 --> 00:05:44,106
Yep.

88
00:05:44,106 --> 00:05:45,806
It's the newest head mount display

89
00:05:45,806 --> 00:05:48,126
from a game development company called Large Heart,

90
00:05:48,126 --> 00:05:49,566
and it hasn't even been released.

91
00:05:50,006 --> 00:05:50,986
But when it finally is,

92
00:05:51,046 --> 00:05:52,326
these things are going to be huge.

93
00:05:52,746 --> 00:05:54,286
Also included is the demo version

94
00:05:54,286 --> 00:05:55,546
of this exclusive software.

95
00:05:56,026 --> 00:05:57,366
It's basically the greatest

96
00:05:57,366 --> 00:05:59,866
3D interactive fantasy video game ever created,

97
00:06:00,006 --> 00:06:01,886
and it's called Romancing Saga 14.

98
00:06:02,686 --> 00:06:03,426
Why Saga?

99
00:06:03,946 --> 00:06:05,926
Because that's the prefecture they live in.

100
00:06:06,066 --> 00:06:06,846
That's the reason?

101
00:06:06,846 --> 00:06:07,166
Yeah.

102
00:06:11,366 --> 00:06:12,366
It's pitch black.

103
00:06:12,366 --> 00:06:13,486
I can't see a thing.

104
00:06:13,706 --> 00:06:14,266
Be patient.

105
00:06:14,386 --> 00:06:15,486
The software's still loading.

106
00:06:15,786 --> 00:06:17,066
It won't be much longer now.

107
00:06:30,566 --> 00:06:33,006
Saga, it is the final frontier.

108
00:06:33,006 --> 00:06:34,966
Uh, that's not cool.

109
00:06:35,306 --> 00:06:36,726
To bring an end to this world,

110
00:06:36,886 --> 00:06:39,106
the reigning governor of Saga took action.

111
00:06:39,606 --> 00:06:41,346
He summoned the Prince of Darkness

112
00:06:41,346 --> 00:06:42,506
from another dimension

113
00:06:42,506 --> 00:06:45,166
in order to destroy the Earth.

114
00:06:46,626 --> 00:06:47,826
The opening is long,

115
00:06:47,906 --> 00:06:48,866
so Rika will skip it.

116
00:06:48,906 --> 00:06:50,066
Hey, don't do that.

117
00:06:50,086 --> 00:06:52,266
I was really interested in the Valhalla Castle.

118
00:06:52,446 --> 00:06:53,386
Sorry, too late.

119
00:06:53,726 --> 00:06:55,086
First, you have to pick a profession,

120
00:06:55,286 --> 00:06:56,946
and that'll determine the specific attributes

121
00:06:56,946 --> 00:06:57,766
of your characters.

122
00:06:57,766 --> 00:06:59,386
Valhalla Castle.

123
00:07:02,946 --> 00:07:04,986
Right, so...

124
00:07:04,986 --> 00:07:06,826
maybe I'll be this.

125
00:07:08,866 --> 00:07:09,346
Oh!

126
00:07:10,786 --> 00:07:11,986
Hey, over here!

127
00:07:12,206 --> 00:07:12,426
Huh?

128
00:07:14,246 --> 00:07:15,066
Oh, wow.

129
00:07:15,286 --> 00:07:16,766
That's some outfit you got there.

130
00:07:17,086 --> 00:07:18,106
Rika chose Gunner,

131
00:07:18,146 --> 00:07:19,206
and this is what it gave her.

132
00:07:19,646 --> 00:07:21,526
You don't look half bad yourself, Kotaka.

133
00:07:21,726 --> 00:07:22,586
Wish I could see.

134
00:07:23,046 --> 00:07:23,626
You can.

135
00:07:23,826 --> 00:07:25,746
Just select equipment from the main menu,

136
00:07:25,866 --> 00:07:27,246
and it'll show you what you look like.

137
00:07:27,766 --> 00:07:30,266
What the hell is this?

138
00:07:30,826 --> 00:07:31,946
I chose wizard.

139
00:07:32,066 --> 00:07:33,506
Wizards don't dress like this.

140
00:07:34,006 --> 00:07:35,506
Rika read about this urban legend

141
00:07:35,506 --> 00:07:37,586
that says if you stay a virgin until you're 30,

142
00:07:37,646 --> 00:07:39,006
you automatically become a wizard.

143
00:07:39,426 --> 00:07:41,246
Rika thinks you look just about right.

144
00:07:41,726 --> 00:07:44,246
Clearly, your character made it to 30 without doing it.

145
00:07:44,386 --> 00:07:45,986
I don't want to be that kind of wizard.

146
00:07:46,146 --> 00:07:47,346
Come on, this is ridiculous.

147
00:07:47,486 --> 00:07:48,986
My guy doesn't even know any magic.

148
00:07:49,326 --> 00:07:51,446
Rika would guess it is perhaps an honorary title.

149
00:07:51,786 --> 00:07:53,646
Is this some sick practical joke?

150
00:07:53,786 --> 00:07:55,266
Hey, what's up with your outfit?

151
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:55,866
Uh...

152
00:07:55,866 --> 00:08:03,406
I wouldn't talk if I were you at all.

153
00:08:03,626 --> 00:08:03,906
Huh?

154
00:08:04,326 --> 00:08:05,886
Uh, wait just a second.

155
00:08:07,426 --> 00:08:09,246
What the hell stupid outfit is this?

156
00:08:09,326 --> 00:08:10,286
I chose blacksmith.

157
00:08:10,666 --> 00:08:11,666
Now that you mention it,

158
00:08:11,666 --> 00:08:12,966
it does sort of look like that.

159
00:08:13,146 --> 00:08:14,206
Please, it does not.

160
00:08:14,426 --> 00:08:15,786
I don't remember blacksmiths

161
00:08:15,786 --> 00:08:17,126
dressing all bloody like this.

162
00:08:17,126 --> 00:08:19,966
They can call forth swords using magic

163
00:08:19,966 --> 00:08:22,026
and cut their enemies to pieces.

164
00:08:22,666 --> 00:08:24,966
Actually, that sounds more like a ninja to Rika.

165
00:08:25,086 --> 00:08:26,526
Oh, man, I screwed up.

166
00:08:26,866 --> 00:08:28,406
I picked the worst possible job

167
00:08:28,406 --> 00:08:29,886
with the worst possible outfit.

168
00:08:30,646 --> 00:08:32,066
Would you quit your bitchy meat?

169
00:08:32,486 --> 00:08:34,106
Uh, what are you?

170
00:08:34,106 --> 00:08:43,786
I picked Rose Girl, and look what it did to me.

171
00:08:44,286 --> 00:08:46,146
Looks like the developer got a little lazy

172
00:08:46,146 --> 00:08:47,166
when he built that one.

173
00:08:47,486 --> 00:08:49,526
But still, check out your attack prowess

174
00:08:49,526 --> 00:08:50,486
and your magic ability.

175
00:08:50,646 --> 00:08:51,546
They're through the roof.

176
00:08:52,006 --> 00:08:52,226
Hmm.

177
00:08:52,586 --> 00:08:54,326
As long as I'm still strong, I'm okay.

178
00:08:55,106 --> 00:08:55,286
Hmm.

179
00:08:55,906 --> 00:08:56,146
Hmm.

180
00:08:56,766 --> 00:08:59,246
You really are in love with that costume, aren't you?

181
00:09:00,006 --> 00:09:00,246
Hmm.

182
00:09:00,566 --> 00:09:01,166
Not really.

183
00:09:01,526 --> 00:09:02,266
Hey, you guys.

184
00:09:02,306 --> 00:09:03,746
What do you think about my outfit?

185
00:09:04,246 --> 00:09:06,566
Well, you, uh, you look very strong.

186
00:09:06,846 --> 00:09:08,786
You're a very authentic-looking samurai.

187
00:09:09,446 --> 00:09:10,366
Hold on a sec.

188
00:09:10,686 --> 00:09:12,086
Senna, Yozara, and Yukimura

189
00:09:12,086 --> 00:09:13,286
are obviously the muscle,

190
00:09:13,666 --> 00:09:15,326
and Rika's the long-distance attacker.

191
00:09:15,646 --> 00:09:16,206
What am I?

192
00:09:16,366 --> 00:09:18,346
If Rika had to make an educated guess,

193
00:09:18,526 --> 00:09:19,046
you're worthless.

194
00:09:19,646 --> 00:09:21,586
That's not the answer I was hoping for.

195
00:09:22,286 --> 00:09:24,886
I guess the only thing we're missing now is a healer.

196
00:09:24,886 --> 00:09:25,706
Don't worry, guys.

197
00:09:25,746 --> 00:09:26,206
I'm here.

198
00:09:26,306 --> 00:09:26,486
Huh?

199
00:09:27,466 --> 00:09:27,906
Maria?

200
00:09:28,726 --> 00:09:31,406
You look exactly the same as you do in real life.

201
00:09:31,746 --> 00:09:33,606
So I'm guessing you're the healer, then.

202
00:09:33,766 --> 00:09:34,046
Yep.

203
00:09:34,186 --> 00:09:35,446
I've seen that look before.

204
00:09:35,986 --> 00:09:38,666
An acolyte of God is always an acolyte of God,

205
00:09:38,706 --> 00:09:39,506
no matter what!

206
00:09:41,146 --> 00:09:43,066
Since everybody is accounted for now,

207
00:09:43,146 --> 00:09:44,066
should we get a move on?

208
00:09:47,906 --> 00:09:49,506
Guys, check it out!

209
00:09:49,706 --> 00:09:50,926
That's Valhalla Castle.

210
00:09:50,926 --> 00:09:52,646
The Prince of Darkness lives here.

211
00:09:52,646 --> 00:09:54,726
This mode is a simulation that ends

212
00:09:54,726 --> 00:09:55,886
after you defeat the bad guy.

213
00:09:56,326 --> 00:09:58,766
This Prince guy can be beaten in a simulation?

214
00:09:59,226 --> 00:10:00,406
Remember what you're wearing?

215
00:10:00,526 --> 00:10:01,686
This game kind of blows.

216
00:10:06,486 --> 00:10:08,006
Looks like we've got company.

217
00:10:08,586 --> 00:10:09,586
What are they, aliens?

218
00:10:09,766 --> 00:10:10,946
They're completely disgusting.

219
00:10:11,286 --> 00:10:12,646
They look and smell like poo.

220
00:10:15,126 --> 00:10:16,226
I know them.

221
00:10:16,886 --> 00:10:18,126
They're dragon gobies.

222
00:10:18,126 --> 00:10:18,846
Hold on.

223
00:10:19,086 --> 00:10:20,406
What the heck's a dragon goby?

224
00:10:20,806 --> 00:10:23,386
Fish that inhabit the Ariake Sea and Kyushu.

225
00:10:23,886 --> 00:10:25,426
I used to eat them when I lived there.

226
00:10:26,126 --> 00:10:28,066
They don't seem very appetizing.

227
00:10:28,606 --> 00:10:29,806
Of course, to each his own.

228
00:10:30,606 --> 00:10:32,246
They're dragon goby soldiers,

229
00:10:32,486 --> 00:10:33,686
the first of the small fry.

230
00:10:34,066 --> 00:10:35,486
The only reason they're in the game

231
00:10:35,486 --> 00:10:36,646
is because they look like aliens.

232
00:10:37,186 --> 00:10:38,266
Man, that's terrible.

233
00:10:38,506 --> 00:10:40,266
I don't care what they are or why they're here.

234
00:10:40,326 --> 00:10:41,066
Let's kill them.

235
00:10:41,326 --> 00:10:42,246
No, stop it.

236
00:10:42,486 --> 00:10:43,786
Don't you feel sorry for them

237
00:10:43,786 --> 00:10:44,906
being treated like monsters

238
00:10:44,906 --> 00:10:46,106
because of how they look?

239
00:10:46,106 --> 00:10:47,946
Dragon gobies may be weird looking,

240
00:10:48,066 --> 00:10:49,946
but they didn't ask to be born that way.

241
00:10:50,406 --> 00:10:51,826
Please, don't hurt them.

242
00:10:51,906 --> 00:10:52,786
Just let them go.

243
00:10:54,526 --> 00:10:55,986
You're a very good man

244
00:10:55,986 --> 00:10:57,386
with a big heart of gold.

245
00:10:57,646 --> 00:10:58,766
When you look at those fish,

246
00:10:58,846 --> 00:11:00,066
you see yourself, don't you?

247
00:11:00,366 --> 00:11:01,726
People as good as you,

248
00:11:02,006 --> 00:11:03,086
they're hard to find.

249
00:11:03,286 --> 00:11:05,426
Yeah, you're really the best, Kodaka.

250
00:11:06,066 --> 00:11:06,406
Oh.

251
00:11:07,726 --> 00:11:08,606
Thanks, guys.

252
00:11:11,026 --> 00:11:11,906
Eat this!

253
00:11:11,906 --> 00:11:15,666
Ah, poor little fish.

254
00:11:15,986 --> 00:11:17,126
Why are you killing them?

255
00:11:17,206 --> 00:11:19,086
What did they ever do to you do, huh?

256
00:11:19,446 --> 00:11:19,666
Huh?

257
00:11:19,906 --> 00:11:20,826
Come on, they're broke.

258
00:11:21,466 --> 00:11:22,586
Rika knows how you feel,

259
00:11:22,826 --> 00:11:24,386
but we can't move on till they're toast.

260
00:11:24,846 --> 00:11:26,606
Their deaths will not be in vain.

261
00:11:26,906 --> 00:11:28,606
They will live on inside each of us

262
00:11:28,606 --> 00:11:30,046
as experience points.

263
00:11:30,546 --> 00:11:31,346
Be gone, demon!

264
00:11:31,346 --> 00:11:36,406
It's samurai mercy.

265
00:11:39,266 --> 00:11:41,226
How come they aren't defending themselves?

266
00:11:41,306 --> 00:11:43,166
They're working out a few kinks in the program.

267
00:11:43,386 --> 00:11:44,526
Rika guesses the developer

268
00:11:44,526 --> 00:11:46,646
forgot to code in the enemy attack patterns.

269
00:11:46,926 --> 00:11:47,306
Oh.

270
